6-DESIGN APPLICATION-SCALE TABLE (NC 58-cluster community college network)
Source: application/results/full/application_full_results.rds$summary_results
Filtered to design_id in {1,2,4,5,6,8} (the 6 retained manuscript designs),
tau = 1.0, averaged over gamma/rho/spillover_type.

NOTE (relabeling): the application study's design_id 1 is named
'Block Stratified Sampling' (application_designs.R), not 'Checkerboard' --
the Checkerboard concept was adapted to a block-stratified analog for the
irregular NC geography. Design_id 8 is similarly named 'Incidence-Guided
Saturation Regions' in the application code (vs. 'Incidence-Guided
Saturation Quadrants' in the grid study) for the same reason -- 'regions'
(k-means clusters) replace the literal 2x2 grid quadrants on the irregular
map. Both are the application study's own names, used verbatim below.
